[
  {
    "id" : "array-items",
    "level" : "Warning",
    "category" : "ErrorProne",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Enforce Array Items Field Presence",
    "description" : "Ensures that schemas with type 'array' include a sibling 'items' field defining the type of the array elements.",
    "explanation" : "# array-items\n\nSchemas with `type: array`, require a sibling `items` field.\n\n**Recommended:** Yes\n\n**Good Example**\n\n```yaml\nTheGoodModel:\n  type: object\n  properties:\n    favoriteColorSets:\n      type: array\n      items:\n        type: array\n        items: {}\n```\n\n**Bad Example**\n\n```yaml\nTheBadModel:\n  type: object\n  properties:\n    favoriteColorSets:\n      type: array\n      items:\n        type: array\n```",
    "enabled" : true,
    "timeToFix" : 5,
    "parameters" : [
    ],
    "languages" : [
    ]
  },
  {
    "id" : "asyncapi-3-channel-no-empty-parameter",
    "level" : "High",
    "category" : "ErrorProne",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Disallow Empty Parameter Substitution in AsyncAPI Channel Addresses",
    "description" : "Ensures that channel addresses in AsyncAPI specifications do not contain empty parameter substitution patterns.",
    "explanation" : "# asyncapi-3-channel-no-empty-parameter\n\nChannel address parameter declarations cannot be empty, ex.`/given/{}` is invalid.\n\n**Recommended:** Yes",
    "enabled" : true,
    "timeToFix" : 5,
    "parameters" : [
    ],
    "languages" : [
    ]
  },
  {
    "id" : "asyncapi-3-channel-no-query-nor-fragment",
    "level" : "Warning",
    "category" : "Compatibility",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Disallow Query or Fragment Delimiters in AsyncAPI Channel Addresses",
    "description" : "Ensures that AsyncAPI channel addresses do not include query parameters ('?') or fragment ('#') delimiters.",
    "explanation" : "# asyncapi-3-channel-no-query-nor-fragment\n\nQuery parameters and fragments shouldn't be used in channel address. Instead, use bindings to define them, ex.`/given?test` is invalid.\n\n**Recommended:** Yes",
    "enabled" : true,
    "timeToFix" : 5,
    "parameters" : [
    ],
    "languages" : [
    ]
  },
  {
    "id" : "asyncapi-3-channel-no-trailing-slash",
    "level" : "Warning",
    "category" : "BestPractice",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Disallow Trailing Slash in AsyncAPI Channel Address",
    "description" : "Ensures that the channel address in AsyncAPI documents does not end with a trailing slash.",
    "explanation" : "# asyncapi-3-channel-no-trailing-slash\n\nKeep trailing slashes off of channel address, as it can cause some confusion. Most messaging protocols will treat `example/foo` and `example/foo/` as different things. Keep in mind that tooling may replace slashes (`/`) with protocol-specific notation (e.g.: `.` for AMQP), therefore, a trailing slash may result in an invalid channel address in some protocols.\n\n**Recommended:** Yes",
    "enabled" : true,
    "timeToFix" : 3,
    "parameters" : [
    ],
    "languages" : [
    ]
  },
  {
    "id" : "asyncapi-3-channel-servers",
    "level" : "Info",
    "category" : "BestPractice",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Enforce Channel Servers Defined in Servers Object",
    "description" : "Ensures that channel servers are defined only in the \"servers\" object of an AsyncAPI document.",
    "explanation" : "# asyncapi-3-channel-servers\n\nChannel servers must be defined in the `servers` object.\n\n**Bad Example**\n\n```yaml\nasyncapi: \"3.0.0\"\ninfo:\n  title: Awesome API\n  description: A very well-defined API\n  version: \"1.0\"\nservers:\n  production:\n    url: \"stoplight.io\"\n    protocol: \"https\"\nchannels:\n  hello:\n    servers:\n      - $ref: #/servers/development\n```\n\n**Good Example**\n\n```yaml\nasyncapi: \"3.0.0\"\ninfo:\n  title: Awesome API\n  description: A very well-defined API\n  version: \"1.0\"\nservers:\n  production:\n    url: \"stoplight.io\"\n    protocol: \"https\"\nchannels:\n  hello:\n    servers:\n      - $ref: #/servers/production\n```\n\n**Recommended:** Yes",
    "enabled" : true,
    "timeToFix" : 5,
    "parameters" : [
    ],
    "languages" : [
    ]
  },
  {
    "id" : "asyncapi-3-document-resolved",
    "level" : "High",
    "category" : "ErrorProne",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Validate AsyncAPI v3 Document Structure After Reference Resolution",
