  {
    "id" : "asyncapi-info-contact",
    "level" : "Info",
    "category" : "BestPractice",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Enforce Info Object to Have Contact Object",
    "description" : "Ensures the Info object in an AsyncAPI document includes a contact object.",
    "explanation" : "# asyncapi-info-contact\n\nInfo object should contain `contact` object.\n\nHopefully, your API description document is so good that nobody ever needs to contact you with questions, but that is rarely the case. The contact object has a few different options for contact details.\n\n**Recommended:** Yes\n\n**Good Example**\n\n```yaml\nasyncapi: \"2.0.0\"\ninfo:\n  title: Awesome API\n  version: \"1.0\"\n  contact:\n    name: A-Team\n    email: a-team@goarmy.com\n```",
    "enabled" : true,
    "timeToFix" : 3,
    "parameters" : [
    ],
    "languages" : [
    ]
  },
  {
    "id" : "asyncapi-info-contact-properties",
    "level" : "Info",
    "category" : "BestPractice",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Enforce AsyncAPI Info Contact Properties",
    "description" : "Ensures the contact object in AsyncAPI info contains the properties \"name\", \"url\", and \"email\".",
    "explanation" : "# asyncapi-info-contact-properties\n\nThe [asyncapi-info-contact](#asyncapi-info-contact) rule will ask you to put in a contact object, and this rule will make sure it's full of the most useful properties: `name`, `url`, and `email`.\n\nPutting in the name of the developer/team/department/company responsible for the API, along with the support email and help-desk/GitHub Issues/whatever URL means people know where to go for help. This can mean more money in the bank, instead of developers just wandering off or complaining online.\n\n**Recommended:** Yes\n\n**Good Example**\n\n```yaml\nasyncapi: \"2.0.0\"\ninfo:\n  title: Awesome API\n  description: A very well-defined API\n  version: \"1.0\"\n  contact:\n    name: A-Team\n    email: a-team@goarmy.com\n    url: https://goarmy.com/apis/support\n```",
    "enabled" : true,
    "timeToFix" : 5,
    "parameters" : [
    ],
    "languages" : [
    ]
  },
  {
    "id" : "asyncapi-info-description",
    "level" : "Info",
    "category" : "Documentation",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Enforce AsyncAPI Info Description Presence and Non-Empty String",
    "description" : "Ensures that the AsyncAPI object contains an 'info' section with a non-empty 'description' string.",
    "explanation" : "# asyncapi-info-description\n\nAsyncAPI object info `description` must be present and non-empty string.\n\nExamples can contain Markdown so you can really go to town with them, implementing getting started information like where to find authentication keys, and how to use them.\n\n**Recommended:** Yes\n\n**Good Example**\n\n```yaml\nasyncapi: \"2.0.0\"\ninfo:\n  version: \"1.0.0\"\n  title: Descriptive API\n  description: >+\n    Some description about the general point of this API, and why it exists when another similar but different API also exists.\n```",
    "enabled" : true,
    "timeToFix" : 3,
    "parameters" : [
    ],
    "languages" : [
    ]
  },
  {
    "id" : "asyncapi-info-license",
    "level" : "Info",
    "category" : "BestPractice",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Enforce License Object in AsyncAPI Info Object",
    "description" : "Ensures that the AsyncAPI 'info' object includes a 'license' object specifying the license information.",
    "explanation" : "# asyncapi-info-license\n\nThe `info` object should have a `license` key.\n\nIt can be hard to pick a license, so if you don't have a lawyer around you can use [TLDRLegal](https://tldrlegal.com/) and [Choose a License](https://choosealicense.com/) to help give you an idea.\n\nHow useful this is in court is not entirely known, but having a license is better than not having a license.\n\n**Recommended:** Yes\n\n**Good Example**\n\n```yaml\nasyncapi: \"2.0.0\"\ninfo:\n  license:\n    name: MIT\n```",
    "enabled" : true,
    "timeToFix" : 5,
    "parameters" : [
    ],
    "languages" : [
    ]
  },
  {
    "id" : "asyncapi-info-license-url",
    "level" : "Info",
    "category" : "BestPractice",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Require License URL in AsyncAPI Info Object",
    "description" : "Ensures that the license object in the AsyncAPI info section includes a URL pointing to the full license text.",
    "explanation" : "# asyncapi-info-license-url\n\nMentioning a license is only useful if people know what the license means, so add a link to the full text for those who need it.\n\n**Recommended:** No\n\n**Good Example**\n\n```yaml\nasyncapi: \"2.0.0\"\ninfo:\n  license:\n    name: MIT\n    url: https://www.tldrlegal.com/l/mit\n```",
    "enabled" : false,
    "timeToFix" : 3,
    "parameters" : [
    ],
    "languages" : [
    ]
  },
  {
    "id" : "asyncapi-latest-version",
    "level" : "Warning",
    "category" : "Compatibility",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Enforce Using Latest AsyncAPI Version",
    "description" : "Checks if the AsyncAPI document is using the latest version of the AsyncAPI specification.",
    "explanation" : "# asyncapi-latest-version\n\nChecking if the AsyncAPI document is using the latest version.\n\n**Recommended:** Yes",
    "enabled" : true,
    "timeToFix" : 5,
    "parameters" : [
    ],
    "languages" : [
    ]
  },
  {
    "id" : "asyncapi-message-examples",
    "level" : "Warning",
    "category" : "ErrorProne",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Enforce AsyncAPI Message Examples to Follow Payload and Headers Schemas",
    "description" : "Ensure that examples in AsyncAPI message objects conform to the defined payload and headers schemas.",
    "explanation" : "# asyncapi-message-examples\n\nAll `examples` in message object should follow `payload` and `headers` schemas.\n\n**Bad Example**\n\n```yaml\nasyncapi: \"2.0.0\"\ninfo:\n  title: Bad API\n  version: \"1.0.0\"\ncomponents:\n  messages:\n    someMessage:\n      payload:\n        type: string\n      headers:\n        type: object\n      examples:\n        - payload: 2137\n          headers: someHeader\n```\n\n**Good Example**\n\n```yaml\nasyncapi: \"2.0.0\"\ninfo:\n  title: Good API\n  version: \"1.0.0\"\ncomponents:\n  messages:\n    someMessage:\n      payload:\n        type: string\n      headers:\n        type: object\n      examples:\n        - payload: foobar\n          headers:\n            someHeader: someValue\n```\n\n**Recommended:** Yes",
    "enabled" : true,
    "timeToFix" : 5,
    "parameters" : [
    ],
    "languages" : [
    ]
  },
  {
    "id" : "asyncapi-message-messageId-uniqueness",
    "level" : "High",
    "category" : "ErrorProne",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Enforce Unique messageId Across All Messages",
    "description" : "Ensures that the 'messageId' value is unique across all messages in an AsyncAPI specification, except those defined in components.",
    "explanation" : "# asyncapi-message-messageId-uniqueness\n\n`messageId` must be unique across all the messages (except those one defined in the components).\n\n**Recommended:** Yes\n\n**Bad Example**\n\n```yaml\nchannels:\n  smartylighting.streetlights.1.0.action.{streetlightId}.turn.on:\n    publish:\n      message:\n        messageId: turnMessage\n  smartylighting.streetlights.1.0.action.{streetlightId}.turn.off:\n    publish:\n      message:\n        messageId: turnMessage\n```\n\n**Good Example**\n\n```yaml\nchannels:\n  smartylighting.streetlights.1.0.action.{streetlightId}.turn.on:\n    publish:\n      message:\n        messageId: turnOnMessage\n  smartylighting.streetlights.1.0.action.{streetlightId}.turn.off:\n    publish:\n      message:\n        messageId: turnOffMessage\n```",
    "enabled" : true,
    "timeToFix" : 5,
    "parameters" : [
    ],
    "languages" : [
    ]
  },
