  {
    "id" : "asyncapi-server-no-trailing-slash",
    "level" : "Info",
    "category" : "BestPractice",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Disallow Trailing Slash in AsyncAPI Server URL",
    "description" : "Ensures that server URLs in AsyncAPI specifications do not end with a trailing slash.",
    "explanation" : "# asyncapi-server-no-trailing-slash\n\nServer URL should not have a trailing slash.\n\nSome tooling forgets to strip trailing slashes off when it's joining the `servers.url` with `channels`, and you can get awkward URLs like `mqtt://example.com/broker//pets`. Best to just strip them off yourself.\n\n**Recommended:** Yes\n\n**Good Example**\n\n```yaml\nservers:\n  - url: mqtt://example.com\n  - url: mqtt://example.com/broker\n```\n\n**Bad Example**\n\n```yaml\nservers:\n  - url: mqtt://example.com/\n  - url: mqtt://example.com/broker/\n```",
    "enabled" : true,
    "timeToFix" : 2,
    "parameters" : [
    ],
    "languages" : [
    ]
  },
  {
    "id" : "asyncapi-servers",
    "level" : "High",
    "category" : "ErrorProne",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Enforce Non-Empty Servers Object in AsyncAPI",
    "description" : "Ensures that the AsyncAPI root object contains a non-empty \"servers\" object.",
    "explanation" : "# asyncapi-servers\n\nA non-empty `servers` object is expected to be located at the root of the document.\n\n**Recommended:** Yes",
    "enabled" : true,
    "timeToFix" : 5,
    "parameters" : [
