  {
    "id" : "oas3_1-servers-in-webhook",
    "level" : "Warning",
    "category" : "Compatibility",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Disallow Servers in Webhook Objects",
    "description" : "This rule enforces that servers should not be defined within webhook objects in OpenAPI 3.1 specifications.",
    "explanation" : "# oas3_1-servers-in-webhook\n\nServers should not be defined in a webhook.\n\n**Recommended:** Yes\n\n**Bad Example**\n\nAt the path item object level:\n\n```yaml\nwebhooks:\n  servers:\n    - url: https://example.com/\n    - url: https://example.com/api/\n```\n\nor\n\nAt the operation level:\n\n```yaml\nwebhooks:\n  newPet:\n    post:\n      servers:\n        -url: https://example.com/\n```",
    "enabled" : true,
    "timeToFix" : 5,
    "parameters" : [
    ],
    "languages" : [
    ]
  },
  {
    "id" : "oas3-api-servers",
    "level" : "Warning",
    "category" : "BestPractice",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Require Non-Empty 'servers' Array in OpenAPI Specification",
    "description" : "Ensures that the OpenAPI specification includes a 'servers' property that is a non-empty array.",
    "explanation" : "# oas3-api-servers\n\nOpenAPI `servers` must be present and non-empty array.\n\n**Recommended:** Yes\n\nShare links to any servers that people might care about. If this is going to be given to internal people then usually that is localhost (so they know the right port number), staging, and production.\n\n```yaml\nservers:\n  - url: https://example.com/api\n    description: Production server\n  - url: https://staging.example.com/api\n    description: Staging server\n  - url: http://localhost:3001\n    description: Development server\n```\n\nIf this is going out to the world, maybe have production and a general sandbox people can play with.",
    "enabled" : true,
    "timeToFix" : 5,
    "parameters" : [
    ],
    "languages" : [
    ]
  },
  {
