  {
    "id" : "oas3-examples-value-or-externalValue",
    "level" : "High",
    "category" : "ErrorProne",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Enforce Examples Have Either \"value\" or \"externalValue\" Field",
    "description" : "Ensures that examples in OpenAPI 3 requestBody or response content have either a \"value\" or an \"externalValue\" field, but not both.",
    "explanation" : "# oas3-examples-value-or-externalValue\n\nExamples for `requestBody` or response examples can have an `externalValue` or a `value`, but they cannot have both.\n\n**Recommended:** Yes\n\n**Bad Example**\n\n```yaml\npaths:\n  /pet:\n    put:\n      operationId: \"replace-pet\"\n      requestBody:\n        content:\n          \"application/json\":\n            examples:\n              foo:\n                summary: A foo example\n                value: { \"foo\": \"bar\" }\n                externalValue: \"http://example.org/foo.json\"\n                # marp! no, can only have one or the other\n```",
